# Sized for GitHub. Everything the task needs is tracked EXCEPT the four
# oversized movies listed below, which exceed GitHub's hard 100 MB per-file
# limit. The other 19 .avi (43.9 MB total), all .wav audio and all .png
# images ARE tracked, so a clone is complete apart from those four.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Oversized stimuli: 151.2 MB each, 604.8 MB together. Named explicitly
# rather than matched by a pattern, so nothing else is caught by accident and
# it is obvious what is missing from a clone.
#
# A.avi and B4.avi are referenced by mGLO_conditions_main.txt, so a fresh
# clone CANNOT run the task until these are copied in from the rig.
# A.avi is byte-identical to A4.avi, and B.avi to B4.avi, so only two
# distinct files (302 MB) actually need copying.
#
# To track them instead, set up Git LFS and delete this block.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
stimulus/visual/A.avi
stimulus/visual/A4.avi
stimulus/visual/B.avi
stimulus/visual/B4.avi

# Recorded session data. MonkeyLogic writes recordings to the task root (it
# has no setting for an output folder); they get moved into "data archive/"
# by hand. That folder IS tracked, via .gitkeep, so a clone arrives with
# somewhere to put them -- but nothing inside it is ever committed, since
# recordings are output rather than source and grow with every run.
*.bhv2
data archive/*
!data archive/.gitkeep

# Old leftovers from the folder reorganisation.
[Aa]rchive/

# Generated analysis output, regenerable from the .bhv2 files.
analysis/figures/
analysis/results/

# The day's trial schedule, written by make_trial_order and read back by
# mglo_condition_selector (trial_orders/trial_order_<yyyymmdd>.mat). A new
# file appears every day the task runs, and the selector rebuilds it
# automatically when the day's file is missing, so it is output not source.
trial_orders/

# macOS resource-fork stubs and Finder metadata.
._*
.DS_Store

# MATLAB scratch and config backups.
*.asv
*.m~
*.bak_*
slprj/
